🧩 1. Structure of a Java Program

A basic Java program consists of:

1️⃣ Package (optional)
2️⃣ Import statements (optional)
3️⃣ Class definition
4️⃣ Main method
5️⃣ Statements (logic)

---

📌 Example Program

```java id="ex2k91"
package mypackage;

import java.util.*;

public class HelloWorld {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
    }
}
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔍 Breakdown

🔹 Package

👉 Groups related classes

```java
package mypackage;
```

---

🔹 Import

👉 Used to access built-in classes

```java
import java.util.*;
```

---

🔹 Class

👉 Blueprint of program

```java
public class HelloWorld
```

---

🔹 Main Method

👉 Entry point of execution

```java
public static void main(String[] args)
```

---

🔹 Statements

👉 Actual logic

```java
System.out.println("Hello, Java!");
```

