⚡ 2. Execution Flow of Java Program

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔁 Step-by-Step Flow

1️⃣ Write code → `.java` file
2️⃣ Compile using `javac`
3️⃣ Generate `.class` file (bytecode)
4️⃣ JVM executes bytecode
5️⃣ Output is displayed

---

📊 Flow Diagram

```text id="bq3y6h"
.java → Compiler (javac) → .class → JVM → Output
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔍 Behind the Scenes

🔹 Compilation Phase

✔ Converts source code → bytecode
✔ Checks syntax errors

---

🔹 Execution Phase

✔ JVM loads class
✔ Verifies bytecode
✔ Executes using interpreter/JIT

---

⚙️ JVM Components (Basic Idea)

* Class Loader → Loads class files
* Bytecode Verifier → Checks security
* Execution Engine → Runs code

---

🎯 Important Points

✔ Java is both **compiled + interpreted**
✔ Bytecode makes Java platform-independent
✔ JVM makes it platform-dependent at runtime

